363
00:14:50,570 --> 00:14:53,270
It also has some
support for Builder,

364
00:14:53,270 --> 00:14:54,710
but it's probably more tailored

365
00:14:54,710 --> 00:14:57,140
towards a Yocto implementation.

366
00:14:57,140 --> 00:15:01,340
Is built around the AB dual
redundant image support.

367
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:04,730
There also is some support
for application updates on

368
00:15:04,730 --> 00:15:08,540
specific platforms as of
more recent releases.

369
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:10,400
Its supports signing and it also

370
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:13,800
has the option to
support delta updates.

371
00:15:13,810 --> 00:15:16,655
One unique thing about

372
00:15:16,655 --> 00:15:18,680
Mender as a framework
is that they have

373
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:20,465
their own management server

374
00:15:20,465 --> 00:15:23,960
that's both open source and
available and hosted form.

375
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,730
Rather than having to deploy

376
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:28,670
your own management server

377
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:31,955
to deploy your update payloads,

378
00:15:31,955 --> 00:15:34,535
you could use the one
that they provided.

379
00:15:34,535 --> 00:15:38,360
They have a starter plan
that's free and then

380
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:42,155
a paid plan depending on
how many devices you have.

381
00:15:42,155 --> 00:15:44,690
This is a quick
way to get started

382
00:15:44,690 --> 00:15:47,900
with an update
deployment scheme.

383
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:50,675
In terms of Mender specifically,

384
00:15:50,675 --> 00:15:52,550
it's got all the components
that we talked about at

385
00:15:52,550 --> 00:15:55,070
the beginning of the
class in terms of

386
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:59,960
how the devices laid out
with two different kernels.

387
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:04,205
You can support two different
kernels and file systems.

388
00:16:04,205 --> 00:16:06,630
Then you'd have a bootloader,

389
00:16:06,630 --> 00:16:08,740
U-boot is often one that's used

390
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:11,530
for the platforms
that are supported,

391
00:16:11,530 --> 00:16:13,330
and then some data
